{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"fields":{"description":"The orphan reconciler cancels executions that already finished successfully, which starts a duplicate run and breaks close on merge.\n\nTwo defects combine. First, persist_execution_state upserts with on_conflict_do_update and an explicit set_ mapping that omits updated_at, so the onupdate default never fires and updated_at freezes at row creation. The reconciler grace window therefore measures age since creation rather than age since activity, so any run lasting longer than the grace is eligible the moment its workflow stops being live. Second, the reconciler treats any non-terminal execution with no live workflow as an orphan, but PR_CREATED and AWAITING_PR_CLOSE are states a successful run reaches after its workflow has legitimately ended while it waits on an external pull request event.\n\nObserved on execution intake-ee0f760a, which reached PR_CREATED at 02:40:46 and was marked CANCELLED at 02:41:19, thirty three seconds later, against a grace of one hundred and twenty seconds. Its frozen updated_at was thirty nine minutes old. Cancelling the row then freed the intake active guard, which admitted a duplicate run for the same ticket. Cancelling it also hides the execution from the pull request webhook lookup in services/orchestration/webhook/pr_events.py, which selects non-terminal executions to signal when the pull request closes, so the ticket would never close on merge.\n\nFix both. Refresh updated_at in the conflict update so the grace window measures activity. Carry the execution state on ActiveExecution and skip the states that are expected to have no live workflow, leaving genuine orphan reclamation intact.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The execution upsert refreshes updated_at on conflict, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_execution_persistence.py -k upsert_refreshes_updated_at`\n- [x] The active execution query selects the state column, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_execution_persistence.py -k active_query_selects_state`\n- [x] ActiveExecution carries the execution state, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_execution_reconciler.py -k carries_state`\n- [x] The reconciler leaves a PR_CREATED execution alone, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_execution_reconciler.py -k skips_pr_created`\n- [x] The reconciler leaves an AWAITING_PR_CLOSE execution alone, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_execution_reconciler.py -k skips_awaiting_pr_close`\n- [x] The reconciler still reclaims a dead execution in a working state, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_execution_reconciler.py -k reclaims_dead_working_state`\n\n## Testing\nRun `pytest tests/unit/test_execution_persistence.py tests/unit/test_execution_reconciler.py -q` to prove the upsert contract and the reclamation policy, then `ruff check .` for lint."}},"env_id":"8c3ef925-fbdc-4d88-8d59-f391cf59568c","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1789961104045289001,"uuid":"1bdaca0f-a4ca-401b-8237-9896ecc092e7"}